\par\par \b \uc2 DocMorris\uc2  announces accelerated implementation of its "AI-First" strategy; positive cost savings of at least CHF 15 million per year\b0\par\par\uc2 1,038 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 June 2026\par 07:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2026, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 \f2 DocMorris AG\f28 \uc2 \f2  / Key word(s): Strategic Company Decision \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 DocMorris\f28 \uc2 \f2  announces accelerated implementation of its "AI-First" strategy; positive cost savings of at least CHF 15 \par million per year \par 25-Jun-2026 / 07:00 CET/CEST \par Release of an ad hoc announcement pursuant to Art. 53 LR \par The issuer is solely responsible for the content of this announcement. \par  \par =---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- \par Frauenfeld, 25 June 2026 \par  \par Press release \par Ad hoc announcement pursuant to Art. 53 LR \par  \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 DocMorris\f28 \uc2 \f2  announces accelerated implementation of its "AI-First" strategy; positive cost savings of at least CHF 15 \par million per year\u160\'00\'A0 \par  \par   . Launch of AI-driven optimisation and automation of extensive processes \par   . Efficiency gains of at least CHF 15 million per year targeted \par   . Group-wide reduction of 100 full-time positions \par   . One-off costs of CHF 5 million, with positive earnings contribution already in the second half of the \par     year \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 DocMorris\f28 \uc2 \f2  is consistently driving the development towards a digital, AI-enabled healthcare platform. To secure \par scalability and competitiveness over the long term, the Group is now accelerating the implementation of its operational \par efficiency measures. By specifically optimising and automating workflows across all areas of the company through the \par use of AI, the cost base will be reduced significantly and sustainably. \par  \par As part of these structural optimisations, \f28 \uc2 \f2 DocMorris\f28 \uc2 \f2  is implementing the reduction of around 100 full-time equivalents \par (FTEs) across the Group. The local statutory procedures will be initiated immediately. \f28 \uc2 \f2 DocMorris\f28 \uc2 \f2  will support the \par affected employees during this transition and is offering appropriate severance packages. \par Focus on customer-centric innovations \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 DocMorris\f28 \uc2 \f2  is making targeted investments in the core capabilities that will shape the company's future in the \par healthcare sector. By the use of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 artificial intelligence\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and Agentic AI tools, capacity will be freed up, allowing \par resources to be increasingly directed towards customer-facing services and innovation. The proven pillars for customers \par remain at the heart of the platform strategy: online pharmacy, telemedicine, retail media, marketplace and the AI \par health assistant. \par  \par CEO \f28 \uc2 \f2 Walter Hess\f28 \uc2 \f2  comments: "Today, technology enables us to further optimise workflows across all areas of the company \par and make them more efficient through consistent automation. Together with the recently completed consolidation at our \par logistics center in Heerlen, this initiative represents another systematic step towards increasing profitability. We \par will manage this process in a socially responsible manner and provide the best possible support to the affected \par employees through targeted measures." \par Annual recurring cost savings of at least CHF 15 million \par The implementation of these measures will incur one-off, extraordinary costs of CHF 5 million in the second quarter of \par 2026, which will already have a positive impact on adjusted operating profit in the second half of 2026. These one-off \par expenses will be offset by recurring cost savings of at least CHF 15 million annually, fully phased in by the end of \par 2027. These savings will be 100 per cent cashflow-positive and largely reflected in EBITDA. \par  \par CFO \f28 \uc2 \f2 Daniel W\u252\'00\'FCest\f28 \uc2 \f2  emphasises: "With the announced efficiency improvements, we are additionally strengthening the \par cost-related and organisational foundations for the planned profitable growth in the coming years." \par Positive revenue momentum continues \par As communicated in the press release of 12 May, revenue growth in the second quarter of 2026 further accelerated \par compared to the first quarter, particularly in prescription medicines (Rx) and digital services. \f28 \uc2 \f2 DocMorris\f28 \uc2 \f2  will publish \par further information in a trading update for the second quarter of 2026 on 15 July. The half-year results, as well as \par the impact of the positive business performance and the announced measures on the guidance 2026, will be communicated \par in detail on 19 August. \par  \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 DocMorris\f28 \uc2 \f2  also announces that a Capital Markets Day will take place on 12 November 2026 in Heerlen, Netherlands. The \par invitation with further details will follow in due course. \par \u160\'00\'A0 \par  \par Investors and analyst contact \par Kelvin J\u246\'00\'F6rn, Head of Investor Relations \par Email: ir@docmorris.com, phone: +41 52 560 58 10 \par  \par Media contact \par Torben Bonnke, Director Communications \par Email: media@docmorris.com, phone: +49 171 864 888 1 \par  \par \u160\'00\'A0 \par  \par Agenda \par  \par 15 July 2026     Q2/2026 Trading Update \par 19 August 2026   2026 Half-year results (conference call/webcast) \par 15 October 2026  Q3/2026 Trading update \par 12 November 2026 Capital Markets Day in Heerlen (NL) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 DocMorris\f28 \uc2 \f2  The Swiss-based \f28 \uc2 \f2 DocMorris AG\f28 \uc2 \f2  is a leading company in the fields of online pharmacy, telemedicine and marketplace with strong brands in Germany and other European countries. Deliveries are mainly from the highly automated logistics centre in Heerlen, the Netherlands. TeleClinic is Germany's largest telemedicine platform, connecting patients with more than 6,500 doctors. DocMorris operates leading marketplaces for health and personal care products in Southern Europe. With its broad range of products and services, DocMorris is pursuing its vision of becoming the leading digital health companion for everyone to manage their health in one click. Around 1,600 employees in Germany, the Netherlands, Spain, France, Portugal and Switzerland generated an external revenue of CHF 1,186 million serving over 12 million active customers in 2025. The shares of DocMorris AG are listed on the SIX Swiss Exchange (securities number 4261528, ISIN CH0042615283, ticker DOCM). For further information, please visit corporate.docmorris.com.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Disclaimer This announcement contains certain forward-looking statements about DocMorris AG and its business, either explicitly or implicitly. Such statements involve known and unknown risks, uncertainties and other factors that could cause the actual results, financial position, performance or achievements of DocMorris AG to differ materially from the future results, performance or achievements expressed or implied by such forward-looking statements. DocMorris AG is making this announcement available as of today's date and undertakes no obligation to update the forward-looking statements contained herein as a result of new information, future events or for any other reason.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 End of Inside Information\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Language:     English \par Company:      DocMorris AG \par               Walzm\u252\'00\'FChlestrasse 49 \par               8500 Frauenfeld \par               Switzerland \par ISIN:         CH0042615283 \par Listed:       SIX Swiss Exchange \par EQS News ID:  2353316 \par \u160\'00\'A0 \par End of Announcement  EQS News Service \par =------------ \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2353316\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A025-Jun-2026\u160\'00\'A0CET/CEST\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Image link: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nwr.eqs-cockpit.com/fncls2.ssx?application_id=2353316&application_name=news&site_id=dow_jones%7e%7e%7ebed8b539-0373-42bd-8d0e-f3efeec9bbed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://nwr.eqs-cockpit.com/fncls2.ssx?application_id=2353316&application_name=news&site_id=dow_jones%7e%7e%7ebed8b539-0373-42bd-8d0e-f3efeec9bbed}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 June 25, 2026 01:00 ET (05:00 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Document DJDN000020260625em6p0008f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
