\par\par \b \uc2 Identiv\uc2  to Sell IoT Assets in Strategic Pivot to Physical AI, Weighs Potential Acquisitions\b0\par\par\uc2 By Elias Schisgall \par \uc2 352 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 June 2026\par 23:44\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2026, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 Identiv\uc2  agreed to sell the operating assets of its Internet of Things business to Trackonomy Systems as part of a pivot to focus on its physical \b \highlight22\uc2 artificial-intelligence\b0 \highlight\uc2  and software-as-a-service businesses.\par \par \uc2 The deal covers \uc2 Identiv\uc2 's IoT assets, including a research and development center in Germany and a subsidiary in Thailand, as well as its name and brand, the company said Wednesday. \uc2 Identiv\uc2  will also contribute $25 million in cash and receive $50 million worth of preferred equity in Trackonomy.\par \par \uc2 The companies also entered into a strategic partnership, meant to reach an agreement on collaborating on software opportunities using Trackonomy's physical \b \highlight22\uc2 artificial-intelligence\b0 \highlight\uc2  platform.\par \par \uc2 Physical AI is generally defined as systems that allow machines to perceive and interact with the physical world.\par \par \uc2 Following the transaction, \uc2 Identiv\uc2  new strategy will be to develop a physical AI SaaS business that can work with Trackonomy's platform. \uc2 Identiv\uc2  will remain a publicly listed company on Nasdaq under the symbol INVE, but plans to change its name after the deal is completed.\par \par \uc2 The company said it is evaluating potential acquisition opportunities, focused on compliance SaaS businesses. It plans to complete an acquisition shortly after the closing of the Tracknomy deal, which is expected in the third or early fourth quarter.\par \par \uc2 Identiv\uc2 's board unanimously approved the deal, and its largest shareholder signed a voting agreement to support the transaction, the company said. The deal remains subject to approval by shareholders.\par \par \uc2 After the transaction, \uc2 James Ousley\uc2 , \uc2 Identiv\uc2 's board chair, will become an observer of Trackonomy's board. Trackonomy Chief Executive Erik Volkerink will be an observer of \uc2 Identiv\uc2 's board. \uc2 Identiv\uc2  also plans to streamline its organization structure and add senior leadership with experience in mergers and acquisitions and the SaaS business.\par \par \uc2 The company's board approved an increase in its stock buyback authorization to $40 million, a boost of around $32 million.\par \par \uc2 Write to Elias Schisgall at elias.schisgall@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 June 24, 2026 17:44 ET (21:44 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Document DJDN000020260624em6o0038i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
