\par\par \b \uc2 Top News Today: Stocks Mixed as Consumer Gains Offset AI Losses\b0\par\par\uc2 2,077 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 June 2026\par 22:43\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2026, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 MARKET WRAPS\par \par \uc2 STOCKS: Stocks finished mixed as a selloff in \b \highlight22\uc2 artificial-intelligence\b0 \highlight\uc2  stocks was offset by gains in sectors that benefit from lower fuel costs.\par \par \uc2 TREASURYS: Treasury yields declined amid safe-haven demand.\par \par \uc2 FOREX: The U.S. dollar rose to 13-month highs as traders continued to price in U.S. rate hikes.\par \par \uc2 COMMODITIES: Oil futures fell, dipping below the psychologically significant $70-per-barrel level at one stage, as increased tanker traffic in the Strait of Hormuz counterbalanced a drop in U.S. commercial stockpiles.\par \par \uc2 HEADLINES\par \par \uc2 Micron Revenue Soars on Continued Memory Demand\par \par \uc2 Micron Technology\uc2  reported a more than fourfold increase in revenue in its latest quarter, boosted by continued strong demand for its memory chips.\par \par \uc2 The company on Wednesday reported a third-quarter profit of $28.24 billion, or $24.67 a share, compared with a profit of $1.89 billion, or $1.68 a share, a year earlier.\par \par \uc2 Stripping out certain one-time items, Micron reported adjusted earnings of $25.11 a share. Analysts polled by FactSet were expecting $20.86 a share.\par \par \uc2 Big Banks Ace an Easier Annual Stress Test\par \par \uc2 JPMorgan Chase, Bank of America and a collection of their peers all passed the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 's annual stress tests, a widely expected outcome after regulators last year began disclosing the exam's scenarios and models in advance.\par \par \uc2 The Fed on Wednesday said big banks were equipped to weather severe economic headwinds. After putting banks through a hypothetical situation where a severe global recession leads to significant declines in commercial real-estate and house prices and rising unemployment, bank capital fell only slightly, staying well above the minimum level at which the Fed considers banks to be safe.\par \par \uc2 As a group, the banks would have faced only $708 in total loan losses, the smallest total of any test in the last seven years.\par \par \uc2 OpenAI\uc2 , \uc2 Broadcom\uc2  Develop Custom Chip for AI Inference\par \par \uc2 OpenAI\uc2  and \uc2 Broadcom\uc2  collaborated to develop a custom \b \highlight22\uc2 artificial-intelligence\b0 \highlight\uc2  chip, marking the next step in the ChatGPT-parent's strategy to build out a full stack behind its models and products.\par \par \uc2 The chip, called Jalape\u241\'00\'F1o, was built from scratch specifically for large-language model inference, with the goal of improving efficiency and lowering the cost to serve AI systems at scale, the companies said Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Early tests show that the chip will deliver performance per watt "substantially better" than current state-of-the-art chips, they added. \uc2 OpenAI\uc2  and \uc2 Broadcom\uc2  didn't disclose specific performance measures but said a more-detailed technical report will be presented in the coming months.\par \par \uc2 Memory-Chip Giant SK Hynix Seeks to Raise $29 Billion in U.S. Listing\par \par \uc2 South Korea's \uc2 SK Hynix\uc2  plans to raise more than $29 billion through a U.S. listing, seeking to tap foreign investors to fund its expansion plans as the \b \highlight22\uc2 artificial-intelligence\b0 \highlight\uc2  boom fuels a rush for advanced chips.\par \par \uc2 The world's second-largest memory-chip maker is looking to raise 45.453 trillion won, equivalent to $29.65 billion, by issuing American depositary receipts on the Nasdaq market, according to a regulatory filing to the \uc2 Korea Exchange\uc2  on Wednesday. The company expects trading to begin July 10.\par \par \uc2 The deal would be one of the biggest share sales in history, comparable to \uc2 Saudi Aramco\uc2 's 2019 initial public offering and surpassing Alibaba's U.S. ADR offering in 2014.\par \par \uc2 Qualcomm\uc2  to Acquire AI Software Firm Modular in $3.9 Billion Stock Deal\par \par \uc2 Qualcomm\uc2  agreed to acquire the AI software company Modular for about $3.9 billion, in a bid to make \b \highlight22\uc2 artificial intelligence\b0 \highlight\uc2  faster and cheaper for its customers.\par \par \uc2 The semiconductor company said Wednesday that, as consideration for the acquisition, \uc2 Qualcomm\uc2  expects to issue up to 19.2 million shares of its common stock to equity owners of Modular. That values the deal at around $3.92 billion, based on \uc2 Qualcomm\uc2 's closing price of $204.13 on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The issuance and sale of the shares will be made in a private placement, \uc2 Qualcomm\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 U.S. New Home Sales Fell in May\par \par \uc2 The rate of new home sales fell in May. Here are the main takeaways from the report released by the Census Bureau and the \uc2 Department of Housing and Urban Development\uc2  Wednesday:\par \par \uc2 -Sales of new single-family homes fell to 580,000 in May, from 626,000 in April.\par \par \uc2 -A consensus of economists polled by The Wall Street Journal expected 632,000 sales in May.\par \par \uc2 Prologis Rebuffed in $16.6 Billion Takeover Approach for U.K.'s Segro\par \par \uc2 Prologis\uc2 , the world's largest owner of industrial real estate, said it made a 12.6 billion-pound ($16.63 billion) takeover approach for smaller U.K. peer \uc2 Segro\uc2 , which turned down the proposal.\par \par \uc2 The move marks the latest takeover attempt of a U.K.-listed company by a U.S. suitor as trans-Atlantic dealmaking expands across sectors, depleting the \uc2 London Stock Exchange\uc2  of some of its longest-standing members. \uc2 Prologis\uc2 's approach for \uc2 Segro\uc2  follows American bids for budget airline \uc2 easyJet\uc2 , ingredients maker Tate & Lyle, energy distributor DCC and asset manager Schroders earlier in the year.\par \par \uc2 Segro said Prologis's proposal was opportunistically timed and sought to take advantage of a dislocation between its share price and its prospects accentuated by geopolitical turmoil.\par \par \uc2 Amazon's Zoox Redesigns Robotaxi for Large-Scale Production\par \par \uc2 Amazon.com's Zoox unveiled a redesigned robotaxi that's built for large-scale production.\par \par \uc2 Zoox said Wednesday the new version incorporates several changes to the interior and exterior of the vehicle while keeping its signature carriage-style cabin.\par \par \uc2 Zoox said it plans to move the new robotaxi into large-scale production at its facility in Hayward, Calif., soon, and expects it will become available to riders later this year. The unit could ramp production up to a rate of 100 vehicles a week to support its expansions this year, subject to regulatory approval, it said.\par \par \uc2 Hertz Dampens Guidance Amid Struggling Used-Car Market\par \par \uc2 Hertz Global said its adjusted earnings in the second quarter are shaping up to be on the low end of its expectations after used-car demand was worse than expected.\par \par \uc2 The car-rental company said Wednesday it expects adjusted corporate earnings before interest, taxes, depreciation and amortization will be between $50 million and $80 million. That is within Hertz's projected range, but toward the lower end.\par \par \uc2 Shares dropped 18% to $4.14 in premarket trading Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 How a CFO Shakeup Turned Wendy's Into a Meme Stock\par \par \uc2 Wendy's stock was surging Wednesday after several users on Reddit's WallStreetBets subreddit called for retail investors to buy shares in the struggling fast-food chain.\par \par \uc2 The shares jumped 35% to $8.45. It was more actively traded than red-hot chip makers Micron and Intel in the premarket.\par \par \uc2 Wendy's said it had appointed former Potbelly Sandwich Works Chief Financial Officer Steve Cirulis as CFO and Chief Strategy Officer on Tuesday, as new CEO Robert Wright's turnaround plan takes shape.\par \par \uc2 Agility, Maker of Humanlike Robots, to Go Public in $2.5 Billion SPAC Deal\par \par \uc2 Agility Robotics, a startup that makes humanlike robots used in manufacturing facilities and warehouses, is set to go public in a deal valuing it at about $2.5 billion, its executives told The Wall Street Journal.\par \par \uc2 Agility is set to merge with dealmaker Michael Klein's special-purpose acquisition company, Churchill Capital Corp. XI, and list under the ticker symbol AGLT.\par \par \uc2 TALKING POINT Life Insurers Aren't Just Investors in Private Credit. They're Major Lenders, Too.\par \par \uc2 Insurance companies are exposed to the embattled private-credit industry in more ways than one, according to a new report by Clearwater Analytics, a portfolio management software provider.\par \par \uc2 About one-quarter of the life insurers tracked by Clearwater that hold stakes in private-credit funds also lend money to them. The insurers typically lend $2 to the funds for each dollar of shares they own. This doubling down on the funds amplifies potential investment returns but also increases risks for the insurers, Clearwater said.\par \par \uc2 Disclosures that insurers make to the National Association of Insurance Commissioners can include thousands of individual investments in different documents, making it difficult to identify when they own shares and debt of the same private-credit fund.\par \par \uc2 The findings offer a window into the complex ties between the insurance industry and the rapidly expanding business of private fund managers. Many fund managers, like Apollo Global Management and KKR, now own life-insurance companies, which in turn have become big investors in private credit.\par \par \uc2 Insurers buy private bonds and loans directly but also invest in private-credit funds as a way to easily get exposure to the hundreds of deals that funds bundle together. The insurance industry is regulated by a patchwork of state agencies that are struggling to keep up.\par \par \uc2 The NAIC said in a statement that insurance regulators have access to information "including limited partnerships and lending activities."\par \par \uc2 Private credit is best known for loans to riskier companies but has grown to include mortgage debt and bonds backed by heavy machinery or intellectual property. Insurers are natural buyers of the hard-to-trade investments because they can lock up money from policyholder premiums for years without worrying about payouts.\par \par \uc2 --Matt Wirz and Shane Shifflett\par \par \uc2 Expected Major Events for Thursday\par \par \uc2 05:00/JPN: Apr Indexes of Business Conditions - Revision\par \par \uc2 05:30/JPN: May Tokyo area department store sales\par \par \uc2 05:30/JPN: May Nationwide department store sales\par \par \uc2 06:00/GER: Jul GfK consumer climate survey\par \par \uc2 06:45/FRA: Jun Consumer confidence survey\par \par \uc2 08:00/ITA: Apr Industrial turnover\par \par \uc2 08:30/UK: May Capital issuance statistics\par \par \uc2 10:00/UK: Jun CBI Distributive Trades Survey\par \par \uc2 12:30/US: May Chicago Fed National Activity Index (CFNAI)\par \par \uc2 12:30/US: May Advance Report on Durable Goods\par \par \uc2 24 Jun 2026 16:43 ET  Top News Today: Stocks Mixed as Consumer Gains Offset AI Losses -2-\par \par \uc2 12:30/CAN: Apr Payroll employment, earnings and hours, and job vacancies\par \par \uc2 12:30/US: 1Q Revised Corporate Profits\par \par \uc2 12:30/US: 1Q 3rd estimate GDP\par \par \uc2 12:30/US: 06/20 Unemployment Insurance Weekly Claims Report - Initial Claims\par \par \uc2 12:30/US: U.S. Weekly Export Sales\par \par \uc2 12:30/US: 1Q State Quarterly Personal Income\par \par \uc2 12:30/US: May Personal Income and Outlays\par \par \uc2 12:30/US: 1Q GDP by State\par \par \uc2 13:00/RUS: Weekly International R